{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-723", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/723", "wordCount": 1939, "segments": [{"start": 12.0, "text": "Hello, everyone."}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "My name's Tina."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "I'm an engineer on the"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "Foundation team."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "I'm going over the highlights of"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "the new APIs we added to"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "Foundation."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "Now, let's get started with the"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "API highlights."}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "These are a variety of things"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "we're going to talk about today."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Let's get started with Ordered"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "Collection Diffing."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "It's an API that allows you to"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "compute and code and apply the"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "diff between collections."}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "To illustrate this, I'm going to"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "tell a story."}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "There is a bear string that"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "really wants to become a bird."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "Let's figure out how to do this."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "We notice that the bear has an E"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "and A that the bird doesn't"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "have."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "And it also needs an I and a D"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "from the bird."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "So let's go ahead and remove the"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "E and A and insert an I in the"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "middle and a D in the end."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "So that took two removals and"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "two insertions to transform a"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "bear to the bird."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "You can do this very easily with"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "Ordered Collection Diffing API."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "The diff here is a collection"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "difference type."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "It's a collection of insertions"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "and removals that describe the"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "element that is inserted or"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "removed and the offset of the"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "element in the collection."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "Here it contains two insertions"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "and two removals as we just saw."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "We can apply the diff on the"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "bear to get a new bird string."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "This is a very powerful API and"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "not only works with strings, but"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "any collection types."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "That was Ordered Collection"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "Diffing."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about data and"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "contiguity."}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "Your app may be building"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "pictures or other types of files"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "from the disk."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "Usually, these forms of data can"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "easily be represented by a"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "contiguous area in memory."}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "On the other hand, your app may"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "be downloading data from the"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "internet using dispatch data or"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "URL session, for example."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "This produces bytes that arrive"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "in multiple chunks in different"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "time, and occupy these"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "contiguous areas in memory."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "Prior to Swift 5, struct Data"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "represented both contiguous and"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "discontiguous regions."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "This unified interface was very"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "simple to use, but it also meant"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "that to provide whole buffer"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "access to the underlying raw"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "bytes, we needed to copy the"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "regions into a contiguous area."}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "This meant that the performance"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "may sometimes be unpredictable."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "In fact, we have look at"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "real-world usage of data, and"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "every discontiguous data gets"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "flattened sometime during its lifecycle."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "So from Swift 5 and onwards, we"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "promise that struct Data is a"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "contiguous buffer type."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "And to present this promise in"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "syntax, we introduce the"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "ContiguousBytes protocol."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "Conforming to this protocol in"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "the case that the type offers"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "direct access to the underlying"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "raw bytes in a contiguous"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "manner."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "So you don't need to worry about"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "accidentally flattening your"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "data anymore."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "Now, how are we going to work"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "with other buffer types that"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "don't promise contiguity?"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "We introduce two new protocols"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "by taking struct Data's"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "interface that's independent to"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "contiguity and generalize it"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "across various buffer types, and"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "we arrive at DataProtocol."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "That is a collection of bytes"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "and MutableDataProtocol to offer"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "additional mutability"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "guarantees."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Buffer types offered by"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "Foundation the Swift Standard"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Library and the dispatch"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "framework have adopted these"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "protocols."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "You probably have worked with"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "some of the types, including"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "Data, array of UInt8 and"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "DispatchData."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "We encourage you to adopt them"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "on your types or methods too as"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "a generic constraint."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "compression."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "Oftentimes, you want to make"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "your data as small as possible."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "It could be that your application is running on"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "devices with limited disk space"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "or you need to transmit"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "resources from or to the"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "internet."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "This is a very common task."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "So we added the compression API"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "to data in Swift."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "It is now as simple."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "It's as simple as this one line"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "of code."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "The API also supports four"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "compression algorithms to offer"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "you different balances between"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "speed, memory and compression"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "ratio."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "I believe you can find one that"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "best suits your needs."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "Now, let's move on to units."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "Foundation already supports 21"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "classes to represent common"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "physical units such as length,"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "speed and duration."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "We extended the unit duration"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "class with subsecond precision"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "units up until picoseconds."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "That is a trillionth of a"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "second."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "The unit frequency class uses"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "hertz as a base unit currently,"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "and this year it gained"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "framesPerSecond."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "It's functionally equivalent to"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "hertz but its cemented meaning"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "makes it ideal to represent"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "on-device FPS measurement."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "The UnitInformationStorage class"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "is new. It can be used to represent the"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "amount of digital information."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "The basic units are bits, bytes"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "and nibbles."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "And the commonly used SI prefix"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "and base-2 prefix units from"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "kilo and kibi up until yotta and"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "yobi are also supported."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "You can use it along with"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "MeasurementFormatter to format,"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "say, data size, or you can use"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "it with ByteCountFormatter if"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "you want more exact control."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "And we have more formatters for"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "you."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "You probably have seen strings"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "like these somewhere every day."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Like, the status of a message"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "you sent is read 1 hour ago, or"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "there is a payment due tomorrow."}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "That is a date or time displayed"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "as a relative point to the"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "present."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "It's not very trivial to make it"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "correct for all locales, so we"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "added the RelativeDateTimeFormatter to"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "help you with this."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "And just like other formatters,"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "the return string is locale"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "friendly, and there are multiple"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "styles you can use."}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "Another thing you probably want"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "to format is a list, and we also"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "added ListFormatter to make this"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "super easy for you ."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "It formats a list into a string"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "that uses the correct separator"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "and conjunctions for all"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "locales."}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "Here is another example."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "Say there is an event that's"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "going to occur at three"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "different dates."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "So you probably want to show a"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "string like the top or the one"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "on the bottom that you spell out"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "the name of the month on your"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "Event page."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "And, of course, you want to"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "display those using the correct"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "format and localized name for"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "different locales."}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "This is important, because, for"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "example, in Europe, they usually"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "counting before month in"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "writing."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "You can also do this very easily"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "with ListFormatter."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "It comes with a property called"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "itemFormatter whose role is to"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "format each item in a list."}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "In this case, we want to format"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "a list of dates, and we know"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "that Foundation supports date"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "formatting using DateFormatter."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "So let's use it as our date"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "itemFormatter."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "And this is all we need."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "We're all set."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "This gives your localized"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "strings as the examples on the"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "bottom."}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "You can easily change the date"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "style by setting the property on"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "DateFormatter."}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "ListFormatter works with all"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "formatters, so please take"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "advantage of it and make string"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "localized greatly in your"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "So that was Formatter."}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "Now let's move on to Operation"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "Queue."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "Imagine in your app there are a"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "bunch of background tasks"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "running concurrently."}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "At this moment, the user wants"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "to save the state of this"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "running app, so how would you do"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "this?"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "Well, you want to make sure all"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "the running tasks are finished"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "before you can save."}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "So it might be tempting to do"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "something like this."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "That is you check the number of"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "running operations in the"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "concurrent queue, and if there"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "isn't any, it must mean that"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "everything we scheduled must"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "have finished."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "So we're ready to save, right?"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "Nope, this is wrong."}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "Please don't do this."}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "It's possible that some other"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "tasks are being scheduled at the"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "same time in all their threads,"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "like right after the check"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "passes and before the save"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "happens."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "What you actually want here is a"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "barrier to guard the safe"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "operation and to make sure that"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "no other tasks can run while the"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "app is being saved."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "Something like this."}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "So we're very excited to let you"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "know that Operation Queue now"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "supports barrier."}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "You should add the BarrierBlock"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "and put your saving operation"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "inside the barrier."}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "This guarantees that the save"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "operation is the only task"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "running at that particular"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "period of time, and it only"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "executes when everything"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "previously scheduled is finished"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "and that no other new jobs will"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "run before it's finished."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "Another update we have for"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "Operation Queue is progress"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "reporting."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "Sometimes you may want to track"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "the overall progress of your"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "concurrent jobs and maybe"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "display a progress bar in your"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "UI."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "You can now do this by setting"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "the totalUnitCount on the"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "progress property of the"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "Operation Queue."}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "Each operation you added to the"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "Operation Queue counterbuilds"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "one unit of"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "completion to the overall"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "progress once operation is"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "finished."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "Next up. Filesystem."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "iOS now supports USB and SMB"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "volumes, which is a network"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "filesystem."}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "This means that you should be"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "prepared to handle files that"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "may exist on other volumes."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "So make sure you use"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "FileManager's itemReplacementDirectory when"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "choosing locations to write new"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "file contents to when doing an"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "Atomic Safe-Save operation."}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "Next, be prepared that volumes"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "may disappear completely if the"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "user pulls out the USB drive or"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "you lose network connectivity to"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "an SMB server."}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "So if you choose the memory"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "mapped files when reading data"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "objects, make sure you use"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "mappedIfSafe as your reading"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "option."}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "This will allow the system to"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "map the file into virtual memory"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "but only if the file is located"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "on nonremovable volumes."}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "Accessing files from USB or SMB"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "drive may be tangibly slower"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "than when you access files on"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "the internal drive."}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "So if you're not doing this"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "already, please defer file"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "system access to non-main thread"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "to make sure your app remains"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "responsive."}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "You may need to test file system"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "capabilities before you use"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "For instance, the APFS features"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "that you're familiar with like"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "cloning may not be available"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "when you access external volumes"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "via USB or SMB."}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "You can test for these"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "capabilities in events with"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "various URL resource keys, or"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "you can make sure you're"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "prepared to handle and receive"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "errors."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "You can find more information"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "about this in the What's New in"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "File Management and QuickLook"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "talk."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "Next up. Swift update."}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "Some Swift APIs were designed"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "originally with Objective-C in"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "mind, and we continued to"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "improve them over the years."}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "First is scanner."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "This is the API in Swift 4."}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "It used to use NSString and"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "return objects by reference."}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "In Swift 5.1, we simplify this"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "interface to this one line of"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "code."}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "What's more, the new API uses"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "the string type of Swift so that"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "strings are collections of"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "graphing instead of code points."}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "This means that you can now work"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "on complex sequences with the"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "new scanner API perfectly, such"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "as emojis."}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "Another improvement is"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "FileHandle."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "It used to throw exceptions when"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "errors occur on the underlying"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "file descriptor."}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "This year, we introduced"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "error-based API, so you can now"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "handle the error right away at"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "call sites."}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "The API for writing data now"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "also works with data protocol."}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "It's also optimized to work with"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "noncontiguous data."}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "So these were the highlights of"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "the new APIs."}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "We encourage you to grab the new"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "Xcode and try these exciting"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "features out."}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "When writing new methods to work"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "with binary data, consider"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "making them bound on the data"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "protocol type instead of"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "requiring particular collection,"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "like array of UInt8."}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "If you're displaying dates or"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "lists in your UI with strings,"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "use RelativeDateTimeFormatter or"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "a ListFormatter to makes sure"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "the string work in every locale."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "We urge you to use Operation"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "Queue's barrier to avoid race"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "condition."}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "And if you're using some sort of"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "progress-reporting mechanism,"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "switch to use the one provided"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "by Operation Queue."}]}
